# AGENTS.md — `src/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. Human orientation is in
[`README.md`](README.md).

## Additional constraints

- Keep analysis kernels pure, small, typed, deterministic, and composable.
- Named adapters (`catalog.py`, `settings.py`, or similarly explicit boundaries)
  may read declared files/environment at call time. They may not do import-time
  I/O, orchestrate stages, choose pipeline destinations, or write hidden output.
- File writing and Snakemake adaptation belong in `workflow/scripts/`; deliberate
  repository operations belong in top-level `scripts/`.
- Public functions require strict type hints, numpydoc documentation, and tests.
- Use `pathlib.Path`, explicit `numpy.random.Generator`/seed inputs, and idiomatic
  NumPy/pandas/SciPy rather than implicit globals or hand-rolled array loops.

## Validation

Use test-driven changes for behavioral code. Run relevant unit/property tests,
then the full quality gates proportionate to the task:

```bash
pytest tests/ -q
pytest --hypothesis-show-statistics
pre-commit run --all-files
```

Pure numerical kernels target at least 90% coverage. A public function without
tests, types, and documentation is not complete.
